# Task Y: the legacy static-recomp $4212 polling tick (hPos += 64 per read,
# beamMasterLast unchanged, so the beam stays ahead of the master clock) runs
# only while g_interp_apu_driving is 0, i.e. for reads from compiled code. That
# made the picture depend on which code is compiled: --lle runs the main thread
# on the interpreter (no tick) but the frame-driver interrupt handlers compiled
# (tick: NMI H-blank wait $C0A2EC), while default mode also ticked in compiled
# main-thread code (joypad wait $C0A073, called from $C5017D). The idle run then
# left --lle at f2557 (DRAM refresh 64 clocks off) and showed a different
# picture f7085-~10000. The tick is part of the calibrated timeline (removing it
# everywhere desyncs TAS 6987M at poll 1785), so keep it exactly where --lle
# has it: compiled code inside a frame-driver interrupt (beam_frame_driver.hunks
# interrupt-depth). Compiled main-thread code now polls like the interpreter.
@@ 4212-poll-tick-interrupt-only
<<<<
      if (!g_interp_apu_driving)
        snes_advance_beam(snes, 64, false);
====
      extern int tlk_frame_interrupt_depth;
      if (!g_interp_apu_driving && tlk_frame_interrupt_depth > 0)
        snes_advance_beam(snes, 64, false);
